      "plan_contents": "# Pulse task #2685: W14: Build complete dynamics, distortion and coloration device families\n\nOperation: b797ea5cff3230413b3ff7fc1cf8f4a7\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nPart of Hex native device roadmap #2661, goal 3, version 0.1. Astra assessment: 17 October 2026.\n\nGoal: reusable quality/detector/filter blocks support complete dynamics and nonlinear devices with distinct, measured behavior.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Shared peak/RMS/envelope detectors, channel linking, lookahead, gain laws, attack/release/auto behavior, crossovers, detector filters, true/sample peak policies, oversampling/decimation and wet/dry latency alignment.\n- Complete Compressor/Gate/Saturator feature gaps with W12, then deliver Limiter, Glue Compressor, Multiband Dynamics, Drum Buss, Overdrive, Pedal, Dynamic Tube, Amp, Cabinet, Erosion, Redux, Vinyl Distortion and Roar as separate devices/PR sequences.\n- Treat modeled circuits, crossover character, curves, coloration and feedback as per-device original laws. Cabinet uses W10 assets/W17 convolution as selected; do not relabel one shaper as every distortion.\n- Add reusable transfer/spectrum/gain-reduction/time meters through W07 and bounded telemetry. Freeze/sleep/bypass behavior must preserve declared histories and avoid falsely asserting zero tails.\n- Modes that alter latency or buffer shape use explicit safe transition/admission; retain old projects' laws when adding quality modes.\n\nAcceptance: independent static knee/transfer anchors and dynamic step/envelope tests; spectral aliasing/oversampling and crossover reconstruction metrics; sidechain alignment and channel-link tests; ceiling/headroom/overflow boundaries; parameter edits during signal; resets/bypass/tails. Every mode has persistent controls and meaningful audible integration. Native listening/reference comparison uses level-matched original fixtures with documented tolerances.\n\nSources: current compressor/gate/saturator implementations and docs; lattice latency/tail contracts; official audio reference. Existing originals are reused; old finite tickets stay closed.\n\nPlanning workstream: split implementation into focused PRs as work begins. Related canonical tickets: #2309, #2311, #2313, #2317. Preserve their current scope, versions, status and PR history. Dependency edges order the enabling contracts; downstream production proof is qualified incrementally under W20.\n",
